<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices rose 0.4 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices rose 0.4 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following provisional data:</p>
<p>				    Sep	  Aug	 Sep 1995</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.4	 -0.3	  0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     1.6	  1.6	  2.0</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    114.0	113.6	112.2</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.17    106.4   0.2   -1.1    1.0</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  33.05    108.8   0.5   -0.1    0.6</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.76    125.2  -0.1    0.4    2.3</p>
<p> Energy				8.25    112.3   1.4    1.2    4.7</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.58    126.8  -0.1   -0.5    1.1</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.55    129.5   0.3    0.6    2.6</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.64    110.0   0.0    0.1    1.1</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.06    113.1   0.4    0.0    1.5</p>
<p>Cumulative inflation in the first nine months of 1996 was 1.3 pct, INSEE said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
